WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.352
Wei Zheng was a famous minister of the Tang dynasty, renowned for daring to speak the truth.

00:00:05.702 --> 00:00:08.462
Everyone knew he was never afraid of offending people.

00:00:08.812 --> 00:00:16.084
At court, wherever the emperor had done something wrong, Wei Zheng pointed it out to his face without any politeness.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.906
The great hall suddenly fell quiet.

00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:26.480
Once, Emperor Taizong was so angry he did not want to attend court, saying that one day he would kill this 'country bumpkin'.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.702
The empress soothed him with gentle words, and the emperor slowly calmed down.

00:00:32.052 --> 00:00:39.396
But after calming down, Taizong understood that Wei Zheng acted for the good of the country, and instead valued him even more.

00:00:39.746 --> 00:00:43.082
From then on, ruler and minister trusted each other even more.

00:00:43.432 --> 00:00:53.488
Emperor Taizong once said: with bronze as a mirror, one can straighten one's clothes and cap; with a person as a mirror, one can see one's gains and losses — and Wei Zheng was such a mirror for him.

00:00:53.838 --> 00:00:57.558
The emperor looked into the mirror, smiled, and nodded.

